WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.110
- [Mark] All right, Garrett.
Garrett, where'd you grow up?

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:04.840
Where you from originally?

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.432
- I grew up here in the Bay Area.

00:00:06.432 --> 00:00:09.180
More on the coast rather
than the Bay area, per say.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.690
A little town called, Half Moon Bay.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.460
- [Mark] Yeah, just
South of San Francisco.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.260
- [Garrett] Yes, it's
in between Santa Cruz

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.370
and San Francisco on highway one.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.440
- [Mark] And tell me about your family.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.090
You had both your parents
when you were a kid?

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.418
- Yes, I did. They
divorced when I was five.

00:00:21.418 --> 00:00:23.270
My dad was kind kinda like a rough,

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.630
tough hippie, like biker guy.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.770
And my mom was a like, she
worked for Kaiser hospital.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.680
She's the one who kind of,
the breadwinner who was a,

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.360
you know, she kept things going.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.720
She was the responsible one.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.580
- [Mark] And how would you
describe your childhood?

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.810
- You know, I was a little bit, you know,

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:44.060
it was a little bit rough,
definitely a broken home,

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:47.510
but we at same time, we, you
know, I was fortunate to,

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:49.320
I worked on a fishing boat as a deck hand.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.153
I got to do a lot of things

00:00:50.153 --> 00:00:52.470
a lot of kids don't get to experience,

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.020
I'd say, you know, especially in this day

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.400
and age of video games and
computers and what not.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.213
I was able to experience
quite a few things

00:01:00.213 --> 00:01:02.910
and treats that just a lot of kids

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.230
don't have the opportunity to do.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.220
- [Mark] Did you finish high school?

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.053
- I did.

00:01:06.053 --> 00:01:06.886
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:01:06.886 --> 00:01:09.204
And where'd your life
go after you left home?

00:01:09.204 --> 00:01:12.110
- You know, I also got into
the narcotics business,

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.263
so just of course I'm
moving to California, so

00:01:14.263 --> 00:01:17.570
and the weed industry
blew up and, you know,

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.830
I did quite well for some time

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.310
but I was young and dumb
and the money that I made

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.880
off that, I kinda just had more
fun than saved and put away.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.590
So, you know, I kind of just

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:29.087
it was one big party for a long time.

00:01:29.087 --> 00:01:29.920
- [Mark] Did you do jail time?

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.710
- Yeah, I've done jail
time. Prison time, yeah.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.543
- [Mark] For drugs?

00:01:32.543 --> 00:01:33.376
- Yeah.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.880
- [Mark] And so you're
in the Tenderloin now,

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.793
how long have you been down here?

00:01:36.793 --> 00:01:39.310
- I don't sleep in the Tenderloin
or stay in the Tenderloin.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.130
I try to get in, get out, you know,

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.080
it's where there are some
resources that you can, you know,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.310
like a shower, clean up what
not, but it's a pit, so.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.000
- [Mark] Yeah. So where
do you, where do you stay?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.360
- You know, I stay up on Buena Vista Park

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.680
up on Haight street.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.270
It's kind of a little
bit out of the crowd,

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.600
that way you can actually like, you know,

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.980
have some peace when you go to sleep

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.410
and you don't worry about
losing your stuff every night

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.288
and getting stolen or beat up or whatever.

00:02:01.288 --> 00:02:02.121
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:02.954
- Yeah.

00:02:02.954 --> 00:02:03.787
- [Mark] A lot of the
crazy stuff happens there.

00:02:03.787 --> 00:02:04.620
- Yeah. For sure.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.240
You know, some people you
wonder if they're crazy?

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.040
Are they momentarily homeless,
going through a struggle

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.830
or like a lot of people seem
like they like it out here.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.872
I'm like okay.

00:02:11.872 --> 00:02:15.390
- [Mark] And what, the harder
drug use started for you when?

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:19.650
- Yeah, about 16, 17, you
know, I fit the, once again

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:20.560
I fit the profile.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.164
I got a scoliosis back surgery

00:02:22.164 --> 00:02:27.164
