00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.320
of destruction going, doesn't it?

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:44.153
- Totally.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.850
- And then it's true like,
especially, well I've noticed

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:51.450
if you look at the homeless
population too, it's like,

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.740
a lot of it, I don't know
if it's mental health issues

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:55.406
which is a big one.
- [Mark] That's a big one.

00:08:55.406 --> 00:08:57.068
- But, I definitely say like
80% of the people are addicted

00:08:57.068 --> 00:09:00.240
to some kind of narcotic
or alcohol, whatever it is.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.180
There's a, you know-

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.048
- [Mark] 80%? I would think about 99%.

00:09:04.048 --> 00:09:05.273
- You're right, yeah.

00:09:05.273 --> 00:09:06.106
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:09:06.106 --> 00:09:08.048
- You're right, exactly.

00:09:08.048 --> 00:09:10.750
- [Mark] You can say drug
addiction is the issue,

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.030
but I really think mental health

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.110
is the real issue behind that.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.776
- [Garrett] True.
- [Mark] And then behind that-

00:09:15.776 --> 00:09:16.850
- [Garrett] Self-medicating along with it.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:18.490
- [Mark] The lack of love and childhood

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.210
is the core of it all I think.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:21.530
- [Garrett] Yeah, exactly.

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:22.470
- [Mark] 'Cause you can have two parents

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:24.390
in your life and you
can say they loved you

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:27.017
but you can still grow up to be an adult

00:09:27.017 --> 00:09:28.610
And not feel like you were ever loved.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:29.640
- [Garrett] Totally.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:33.000
- [Mark] I think that's the
most common story I hear.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:33.833
- [Garrett] Yeah.

00:09:33.833 --> 00:09:35.145
- [Mark] Whether the people
understand it themselves or not.

00:09:35.145 --> 00:09:36.515
- [Garrett] Right. I think you're right.

00:09:36.515 --> 00:09:38.546
Common denominator, you know.

00:09:38.546 --> 00:09:39.780
- [Mark] But people would
just say homelessness

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:40.963
and drug addiction is the problem.

00:09:40.963 --> 00:09:42.400
Don't really understand it.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:43.300
- [Garrett] Right.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.223
- [Mark] So do you have people

00:09:46.223 --> 00:09:47.640
on the street here that you trust?

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:49.950
- [Garrett] There's a, I
got a very very small circle

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:53.120
and you know, they're not
really on the street though,

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.010
like I am. Just local
dealers and stuff like that,

00:09:57.010 --> 00:10:00.080
that's got their stuff together, but yeah.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.686
- [Mark] And what kind of
dreams did you have as a kid

00:10:01.686 --> 00:10:03.560
of doing as a job? What things did you

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:04.393
wanna do with your life?

00:10:04.393 --> 00:10:05.633
- [Garrett] I grew up
surfing and I used to be

00:10:05.633 --> 00:10:08.340
in the NSSA as a junior.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.690
But right now, I don't know if you've

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:10.640
ever heard of Mavericks?

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:11.473
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:10:11.473 --> 00:10:12.451
- [Garrett] I should be
surfing right there, right now.

00:10:12.451 --> 00:10:14.330
- [Mark] It's the time of year for it.

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:16.010
- [Garrett] Yeah. It's
yeah, I've been missing it

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.835
and seeing my buddies and stuff, you know

00:10:17.835 --> 00:10:21.700
send me a, show me back on
YouTube what I'm missing

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:22.679
and I'm like, Oh my God.

00:10:22.679 --> 00:10:24.743
- [Mark] And you surf
those big, giant waves?

00:10:24.743 --> 00:10:26.670
- You know I haven't been
to quite those giant waves,

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.740
but you know, ocean beach training ground,

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:29.573
a good place for them.

00:10:29.573 --> 00:10:30.830
But I was well on my way there.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.010
I hope to get back there soon.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:33.040
Get back in shape.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:36.714
- [Mark] Is there also like
a self-destruction streak

00:10:36.714 --> 00:10:39.690
that runs in these guys
that surf those giant waves?

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:41.350
'Cause that's threatening your
life every time you do it.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.210
- For sure. It's certainly
a little healthier though.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:44.043
I mean-

00:10:44.043 --> 00:10:44.940
- [Mark] Yeah, no it's (laughing)

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:47.144
it's probably a healthier form of-

00:10:47.144 --> 00:10:49.318
- Healthier form definitely, yeah.

00:10:49.318 --> 00:10:52.310
- [Mark] I understand challenging
yourself, but that seems

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:53.939
like, a lot of those
guys end up dying, right?

00:10:53.939 --> 00:10:55.210
- Some of them-

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.460
- [Mark] A lot. Well,
I shouldn't say a lot,

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.293
but it's happened?

00:10:58.293 --> 00:10:59.126
- Yeah.

00:10:59.126 --> 00:11:01.100
- [Mark] It also keeps
you in incredible shape.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.370
- Totally. Yeah.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:03.740
- [Mark] Yeah. It's
probably a very healthy way

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:04.573
to challenge yourself-

00:11:04.573 --> 00:11:06.310
- Yeah, it's a lot healthier outlook.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.490
- [Mark] As long as you
don't end up under water,

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:08.950
for too long.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:09.870
- Yep.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:10.740
- [Mark] Excellent.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.840
So where, what do you see your chances

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.460
are of getting outta here, I mean?

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.293
- You know, pretty good.

00:11:16.293 --> 00:11:18.870
I will say that I've
done it before, you know,

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:22.760
and this has gone on far
too long, I'll admit it.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.504
It's going on a year now.

00:11:24.504 --> 00:11:26.666
It's supposed to be maybe
two, three month thing

00:11:26.666 --> 00:11:29.280
and you just keep saying next month

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.579
next month, next month, you know?

00:11:30.579 --> 00:11:31.412
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:11:31.412 --> 00:11:32.245
- That's the drugs.

00:11:32.245 --> 00:11:34.480
- [Mark] Just don't let yourself
become a 60 year old man

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:35.990
still living on the street,
you do see a lot of them.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:37.490
- Yeah, yeah. Like I said,
it's even embarrassing for me

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.681
to even be telling you
this stuff, you know.

00:11:39.681 --> 00:11:41.730
I'm much better than this, you know.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:42.730
- [Mark] I can totally see you cleaning

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:44.520
up and getting your,
getting your life straight.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.346
- Yeah, thank you. Yeah,
I'm much better than this.

00:11:46.346 --> 00:11:48.193
- [Mark] What's the most important lesson

00:11:48.193 --> 00:11:49.413
you've learned from all this?

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:54.260
- There's quite a few, you know,

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.310
whether it's through any kind of community

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.260
or any kind of like
support you have, you know,

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:03.043
like use that support
really. Don't neglect it or-

00:12:04.071 --> 00:12:05.020
- [Mark] Take advantage of it.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:06.420
- Absolutely.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:08.950
- [Mark] Well, I see a lot
of people that ask for help.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:09.783
- Yeah.

00:12:09.783 --> 00:12:10.970
- [Mark] And then when
they get offered the help-

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.636
- Yeah.
- [Mark] They can't accept it.

00:12:12.636 --> 00:12:13.469
- Right. That's true.

00:12:13.469 --> 00:12:14.770
- [Mark] And they flake
out and they disappear

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:16.428
and all of a sudden
you're like, here it is-

00:12:16.428 --> 00:12:18.094
- Yeah.
- [Mark] On a silver platter.

00:12:18.094 --> 00:12:18.927
- Yeah, exactly.

00:12:18.927 --> 00:12:19.760
- [Mark] Can't accept it.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.593
- Can't accept it, totally. I see that.

00:12:20.593 --> 00:12:21.659
I see that left and right.

00:12:21.659 --> 00:12:22.510
I can't tell you how
many times I see that.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.100
- [Mark] That self-sabotage
thing kicks in.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.470
- Yeah, big time.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.368
- [Mark] The thing that you
dream about and say you want.

00:12:27.368 --> 00:12:29.150
- Is right here, but you just can't do it.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:29.983
- [Mark] You run away from it.

00:12:29.983 --> 00:12:32.820
- Right. Totally. I'm
definitely guilty of that.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:34.260
- [Mark] I think everybody down here is.

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:35.093
- [Garrett] Yeah.

00:12:35.093 --> 00:12:36.796
- [Mark] I think everybody
in the world is guilty of it.

00:12:36.796 --> 00:12:38.320
One way or another.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.153
- [Garrett] True that.

00:12:39.153 --> 00:12:40.200
- [Mark] We're our own worst enemies.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:41.927
- [Garrett] Yes, we are.
Everywhere we go, there we are.

00:12:41.927 --> 00:12:44.160
(Mark and Garrett laughing)

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:45.310
- [Mark] All right.
Garret, thank you so much

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:46.143
for talking with me.

00:12:46.143 --> 00:12:46.976
- Yeah, I appreciate it.

00:12:46.976 --> 00:12:47.809
- [Mark] I wish you the best of luck, man.

00:12:47.809 --> 00:12:48.814
- Yeah, yep. Thank you.

00:12:48.814 --> 00:12:50.397
- [Mark] Thank you.

